      "id": 1,
      "text": "Klondike, also called Pleasant Grove, sits at the junction of Farm Roads 1528 and 2890, three miles southwest of Cooper in Delta County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/klondike-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1895 the Texas‑Midland Railroad built a line through Pleasant Grove to Cooper, making the settlement a railroad stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/klondike-tx",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name honors the Canadian Klondike gold rush, chosen when Joel Jefferson Hunt applied for a postal franchise in 1897.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/klondike-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A Methodist congregation and school shared a building in the 1860s, and later a Baptist church joined, showing early religious cooperation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/klondike-tx",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Klondike housed two large cotton gins and was a key cotton shipping point through the 1920s, reaching 350 residents by 1929.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/klondike-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Pleasant Grove Cemetery was founded in 1852 when John Hunt donated the land, marking Klondike’s earliest recorded settlement.",
